      "agent_id": "Summary",
      "message": "The main differences between PostgreSQL 17 and PostgreSQL 18 are primarily related to performance improvements and feature enhancements. According to recent benchmarking and comparison sources:\n\n- PostgreSQL 18 offers a noticeable performance boost over version 17, with improvements observed in various real-world query scenarios. Upgrading to PostgreSQL 18 can make many everyday queries run faster without requiring schema changes or application rewrites.\n- The delta between the two versions is relatively small, but PostgreSQL 18 benefits from optimizations that enhance efficiency and speed.\n- Specific features added or improved in PostgreSQL 18 can be found in the official feature matrix, which details new capabilities and changes across versions.\n\nSources:\n- [PlanetScale Benchmarking Postgres 17 vs 18](https://planetscale.com/blog/benchmarking-postgres-17-vs-18)\n- [Cybertec PostgreSQL Stats Comparison](https://www.cybertec-postgresql.com/en/comparing-stats-postgresql-18-against-17/)\n- [Postgres Weekly Issue #620](https://postgresweekly.com/issues/620)\n- [Posette Conference Talk on Performance](https://posetteconf.com/2026/talks/postgresql-17-vs-18-side-by-side-performance-wins-in-real-world-queries/)\n\nIn summary, PostgreSQL 18 provides performance enhancements over 17, with minor feature updates, making it a recommended upgrade for better efficiency.",
